title: Typed records, enums, and modules
---

# Typed Records, Enums, and Modules

## Objective

Describe structured values with record types, optional and default fields,
inheritance and overrides, enum values, and an explicit local module import.

## Prerequisites

Complete [lesson 03](./03_Collections_and_Functions.amx). This lesson has no
mapped data input, but imports the supplied Asset type from
`libraries/asset-management.amx`.

## Desktop workflow

In a project created with **OpenAMX learning guide**, open
`04_Typed_Records_Enums_and_Modules.amx` at the project root and keep its
relative `libraries/` folder in place. If using the repository checkout, open
`examples/04_Typed_Records_Enums_and_Modules.amx` under `examples/`. Select
**Run** to inspect the records and **Preview** to read the explanation.

## Typed values and reuse

The imported `Asset` type is exported by a local module and is not a built-in
language type. That module marks schema declarations with `export type`;
imports expose only explicitly exported names. The local types below show
required fields, optional nullable fields, literal defaults, inheritance, and
the required `override` marker. Enum members evaluate to primitive values;
this enum starts at 1.

```amx
import { Asset } from "./libraries/asset-management.amx"

enum Status = {
  DRAFT,
  ACTIVE,
  CLOSED
}

type Identifier {
  id: String
}

type NamedRecord extends Identifier {
  override id: String
  name: String
}

type ReviewRecord extends NamedRecord {
  reviewedAt?: DateTime? = null
  status: Number = 1
  note?: String? = null
  labels: String[] = ["intake"]
}

let libraryAsset: Asset = Asset {
  id = "A-001",
  name = "North Pump 01",
  assetClass = "Pump",
  criticality = 4
}
let minimalReview: ReviewRecord = ReviewRecord { id = "A-001", name = "North Pump 01" }
let reviewed: ReviewRecord = ReviewRecord {
  id = "A-001",
  name = "North Pump 01",
  reviewedAt = "2026-09-29T12:00:00Z",
  status = Status.ACTIVE,
  note = null
}
```

The imported asset is **{{ libraryAsset.name }}**. Its failure-mode list uses
the module's empty-list default. The minimal review has status
{{ minimalReview.status }} and nullable note {{ minimalReview.note }}; the
reviewed record has enum value {{ reviewed.status }} and timestamp
{{ reviewed.reviewedAt }}.

## Expected outcome

Run reports `libraryAsset.name = "North Pump 01"`, an empty
`libraryAsset.failureModes`, `minimalReview.status = 1`,
`minimalReview.note = null`, and `reviewed.status = 2`. The DateTime retains
its supplied RFC 3339 text. A child record is still a distinct type; an
override replaces an inherited field contract rather than making the child
assignable to its parent.

## Inputs and support files

No external input mappings are needed. The required project-relative
dependency is `libraries/asset-management.amx`; it exports the `Asset` schema
used above. In the repository checkout, that file is
`examples/libraries/asset-management.amx`.

